<title>FRANCE: GEC Alsthom agrees to run Amerail's Hornell site.</title>
<headline>GEC Alsthom agrees to run Amerail's Hornell site.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-08-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>GEC Alsthom said it had agreed to run the Hornell train construction site at Hornell, New York, previously owned by the American Passenger Rail Car Company LCC (Amerail).</p>
<p>GEC Alsthom signed the agreement with the Fidelity and Deposit Company of Maryland. Under the deal, the Industrial Development Agency of Hornell will rent the workshops and offices to GEC Alsthom while GEC Alsthom Transportation In will run the the Hornell company.</p>
<p>Hornell employs 170 people.</p>
<p>GEC Alsthom is a joint venture of Alcatel Alsthom and General Electric Co Plc.</p>
<p>-- Paris newsroom +33 1 4221 5452</p>
</text>
